Wen2025.pdf.md:51:First, we estimated individualized gray matter morphological abnormalities by employing the normative modeling. Following methods used in previous studies [18, 20, 24], we trained a Gaussian process regression model to estimate the normative range of regional GMVs from age and sex in HCs according to the brain connectome atlas [37]. This trained model was then applied to each patient to generate predicted GMVs. Subsequently, Z scores were calculated to quantify deviations of the predicted GMVs from normal distributions. Positive Z scores indicated higher GMVs in patients compared to HCs, and vice versa. This process resulted in a Z-score vector (246 × 1) for each patient, representing their individualized gray matter morphological abnormalities.
